Hermes v0.21.4 compatibility review
=================================

Scope: komatso-bale-registry, komatso-user-registry, komatso-session-namer.
No production source or manifest changes are required.

Both v1 plugin.yaml files parse with the target manifest parser. The target
directory loader imports their __init__.py and register(ctx) functions.
PluginContext.register_hook("pre_gateway_dispatch", callback) remains valid.
The callbacks accept additive keyword arguments, run on the caller thread,
and may mutate MessageEvent.text/channel_prompt or return {"action": "skip"}.
The target invokes this hook before authorization. Its turn path still passes
event.channel_prompt onward. No developer grants or permissions were broadened.

PairingStore is_approved/list_pending/approve_request/generate_code/approve_code
and revoke retain the signatures used here. Tests exercise real target pairing
storage in a temporary directory, including failed-approval behavior in the
registration DB. The canonical production DB paths are unchanged.

HOOK.yaml and async handle(event_type, context) match gateway.hooks. The target
agent:start and agent:end payloads retain platform (string), user_id and
session_id. SessionDB accepts db_path and retains get_session_title and
set_session_title. Tests verify Bale/Telegram titles, duplicate-title suffixes,
repeat events and the existing revoked-Bale-user naming restriction.

Offline validation
------------------
test_v0214_compat.py: 10 tests passed on the target checkout with Python 3.11.
The tests use target loader, event, pairing and SessionDB APIs. No gateway is
constructed. Sends and operational menu/report handlers are mocked. Socket
connections and DNS are blocked after Windows event-loop construction. All
test identities are synthetic; all registration/pairing/session state is
redirected to a temporary directory beneath KomatsoAI/runtime and cleaned up.

Reproduce from E:\KomatsoAI, using already available dependencies (read-only):

  $env:KOMATSO_TEST_HERMES_ROOT='E:\HermesUpgrade\hermes-agent-v0.21.4'
  $env:HERMES_HOME='E:\KomatsoAI\runtime\registry-v0214-tests'
  $env:PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE='1'
  .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -B -c "import sys,runpy; sys.path.append(r'C:\Users\win-10\AppData\Local\hermes\hermes-agent\venv\Lib\site-packages'); runpy.run_path('integrations/hermes/plugins/komatso-bale-registry/test_v0214_compat.py',run_name='__main__')"

No install, deploy, restart, live DB access, real messaging, gateway run or full
regression is part of this validation. Live dispatch/configuration, filesystem
ACLs and concurrent production DB use remain untested. Existing permissions
and behavior are deliberately retained rather than refactored. No core patch
is required. Recheck the private loader helpers on subsequent Hermes upgrades.
